---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

const lastUpdated = "21 May 2026";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description={`The terms under which you may use the ${site.name} website and its content.`}
>
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden">
    <div class="hero-blob"></div>
    <div class="relative mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 pt-20 pb-8 sm:pt-24">
      <p class="text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-indigo-600">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pb-20">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 space-y-6 text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        Welcome. These Terms of Service ("Terms") govern your use of the <strong>{site.name}</strong>
        marketing website at <a href={site.url} class="text-indigo-600 hover:underline">{site.domain}</a>
        ("the Site"). By accessing or using the Site you agree to these Terms. If you do not agree,
        please do not use the Site.
      </p>
      <p>
        These Terms cover only the marketing website. Our SaaS products (e.g. TravelERP) have
        separate product terms presented at signup, which take precedence for product use.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-2 tracking-tight">1. About {site.name}</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is a software studio that develops and operates SaaS products and provides
        custom software development services. The Site is informational — it describes what we
        offer and lets you contact us. Engaging us for a service or subscribing to a product
        creates a separate commercial agreement.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-2 tracking-tight">2. Using the Site</h2>
      <p>You agree to use the Site lawfully and respectfully. You will not:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>Attempt to gain unauthorised access to the Site, its underlying servers or accounts of others.</li>
        <li>Interfere with the operation of the Site (DoS attacks, scraping at abusive rates, etc.).</li>
        <li>Submit content through our contact form that is unlawful, defamatory, infringing or harmful.</li>
        <li>Use the Site to send spam, phishing messages or unsolicited commercial communications.</li>
        <li>Reverse-engineer, scrape or systematically extract content from the Site for commercial use without our written consent.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may suspend or block access to the Site at our discretion if we believe these Terms have
        been breached, without notice.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-2 tracking-tight">3. Intellectual property</h2>
      <p>
        Unless otherwise indicated, all content on the Site — text, layouts, code, graphics, logos,
        product names, photographs and the design itself — is owned by or licensed to {site.name}
        and protected by Indian and international intellectual property laws.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may view, share and link to our content for non-commercial purposes with appropriate
        attribution. You may not reproduce or republish substantial portions of our content
        (including blog posts) commercially, or train machine-learning models on our content,
        without prior written consent. Quote responsibly with a link back.
      </p>
      <p>
        Our marks <strong>{site.name}</strong>, <strong>TravelERP</strong>, and the associated logos
        are our trademarks. Third-party names mentioned on the Site belong to their respective
        owners.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-2 tracking-tight">4. Content disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        Our blog posts and other educational content reflect our genuine experience and the best
        information available at time of writing. We provide them for general guidance only. They
        are not professional advice (legal, financial, medical, regulatory, or otherwise) and
        should not be relied on as a substitute for advice from a qualified expert for your
        specific situation.
      </p>
      <p>
        Industry numbers, benchmarks and cost ranges cited in our posts are based on publicly
        available sources or our own deployment experience. They are honest estimates but actual
        results will vary by use case. We are not liable for decisions made solely on the basis
        of our published content.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-2 tracking-tight">5. Third-party links</h2>
      <p>
        The Site contains links to third-party websites and services. We do not control those sites
        and are not responsible for their content, accuracy, security or privacy practices. A link
        does not imply endorsement.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-2 tracking-tight">6. Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        The Site may display advertising delivered by Google AdSense and its partner networks. We
        do not control the specific ads shown to you; they are selected based on your browsing
        history, this Site's content and Google's ad-relevance algorithms. We are not responsible
        for the products, services or content of advertisers. Click and purchase at your own
        discretion. See our <a href="/privacy" class="text-indigo-600 hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>
        for information about ad cookies and how to opt out of personalised advertising.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-2 tracking-tight">7. Availability</h2>
      <p>
        We try to keep the Site available 24×7 but do not guarantee uninterrupted access. The Site
        may be unavailable for maintenance, third-party outages (Cloudflare, DNS) or factors beyond
        our reasonable control. We are not liable for any loss arising from temporary unavailability
        of the Site.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-2 tracking-tight">8. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
      <p>
        The Site is provided on an "as is" and "as available" basis. To the maximum extent permitted
        by applicable law, we disclaim all warranties — express, implied or statutory — including
        warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, accuracy, reliability and
        non-infringement. We do not warrant that the Site will be error-free, secure or free from
        malware.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-2 tracking-tight">9. Limitation of liability</h2>
      <p>
        To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, {site.name}, its directors, employees
        and contractors will not be liable for any indirect, incidental, consequential, special or
        exemplary damages — including loss of profits, revenue, data, goodwill or business
        opportunity — arising from your use of the Site, even if we have been advised of the
        possibility of such damages.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where liability cannot be excluded by law, our total aggregate liability to you arising
        from your use of the Site is limited to ₹1,000.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-2 tracking-tight">10. Indemnity</h2>
      <p>
        You agree to indemnify and hold harmless {site.name} from any claims, damages, liabilities
        and reasonable costs (including legal fees) arising from your breach of these Terms or
        your misuse of the Site.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-2 tracking-tight">11. Governing law and disputes</h2>
      <p>
        These Terms are governed by the laws of India. Any dispute arising out of or in connection
        with these Terms or your use of the Site will be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of
        the courts at Gurugram, Haryana, India, except where mandatory consumer-protection law
        requires otherwise.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-2 tracking-tight">12. Changes to these Terms</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these Terms from time to time. The "Last updated" date at the top of this
        page reflects the latest revision. Continued use of the Site after changes are posted
        constitutes acceptance of the revised Terms.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mt-10 mb-2 tracking-tight">13. Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about these Terms? Reach us at:</p>
      <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
        <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`} class="text-indigo-600 hover:underline">{site.contactEmail}</a></li>
        <li>Phone: <a href={`tel:${site.phone}`} class="text-indigo-600 hover:underline">{site.phoneDisplay}</a></li>
        <li>Web: <a href="/contact" class="text-indigo-600 hover:underline">{site.url}/contact</a></li>
      </ul>

      <p class="mt-10 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200 text-sm text-slate-500">
        These Terms are provided as general informational content. They are not legal advice and
        do not establish a lawyer-client relationship. For advice tailored to a specific situation
        or jurisdiction, consult a qualified lawyer.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
